PyTM30 implements ANSI/IES TM-30-20 from the published standard:

    ANSI/IES TM-30-20, "IES Method for Evaluating Light Source Color
    Rendition", An American National Standard, Illuminating Engineering
    Society, New York, 2020, incorporating Errata 1 (2021).
    ISBN 978-0-87995-379-9. (IES standards are issued without DOIs.)

Spectral data (CES reflectances, CMFs, daylight basis functions, illuminants)
in data/ are CIE datasets, published by the International Commission on
Illumination (CIE) under CC BY-SA 4.0 and distributed here under the same
licence, separately from the MIT code. Per-file source DOIs and the changes
made are listed in data/README.md. The tables were extracted using
colour-science (BSD-3-Clause) as a tool:

    Mansencal, T., Mauderer, M., Parsons, M., et al. (2025). Colour 0.4.7
    [Computer software]. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17837391
    Repository: https://github.com/colour-science/colour
    Website: https://www.colour-science.org

See tools/generate_data_colour_science.py for the extraction of each table.

Numerical accuracy is cross-validated against colour-science (BSD-3-Clause).
No code from any GPL-licensed project is incorporated.

The CES reflectance data and TM-30-20 method originate with the IES and CIE.
